# Rust
/target

# Project local
/.superpowers/
/.worktrees/
/.atl/
/.codegraph/

# Local cargo settings (`jobs = 4` to cap build memory). Deliberately NOT
# committed: available RAM is a property of the machine, not of the project.
# Committing `jobs = 4` would impose a 16 GB developer's memory limit on anyone
# working with 64 GB, tripling their build time for no benefit. CI is unaffected
# either way, since GitHub's windows-latest runner has 4 cores and that is
# already cargo's default there.
# See .cargo/config.toml for the reasoning.
/.cargo/

# Development docs (local-only, not published to the public repo)
/docs/superpowers/
/openspec/
/odd/

# Visual-baseline scratch output from tools/visual/capture.ps1.
#
# `artifacts/visual/baseline/` IS committed: those PNGs are the reviewed
# reference. Everything the tool GENERATES — the current frames, the diff PNGs
# and summary.json — is transient and must never reach the repository. Without
# this line a `git add artifacts/` commits four scratch frames and four diffs
# alongside the baselines, and the next reviewer cannot tell which image is the
# reference.
/artifacts/visual/current/

